note OMC-EFF conductor self-test (PROTOCOL.md, PROTOCOL-2.md, PROTOCOL-3.md), the Omega port of the former
note selftest.sh. It proves the conductor's checks can fail. No measured timing value is printed: wall,
note runtime and counter columns are only tested for presence, and runtime=123 comes from a synthetic
note fixture program.
note
note   selftest OMC HERE SCRATCH
note OMC      absolute path of the omc that builds the conductor, the kernels and the fixtures
note HERE     absolute path of bench/omc_efficiency
note SCRATCH  a directory that must not exist; it is created and becomes the working directory
note
note gcc runs as /usr/bin/gcc -B/usr/bin/ with an empty environment (execprog passes none).
note One line per check: PASS NAME rc=N EXPECTED, FAIL NAME rc=N EXPECTED got LINE, or NOT_RUN NAME REASON.
note Last line: SELFTEST fails=N not_run=N. Exit 0 when fails is 0, 1 otherwise, 2 for bad usage.
note counters_nonzero is NOT_RUN when /proc/sys/kernel/perf_event_paranoid is above 2 (unprivileged perf
note stat cannot count); NOT_RUN is reported, never counted as a pass.
om2
text tcond "conductor"
text tcondom "/conductor.om"
text tkern "/kernels/"
text twant "/want/"
text tom ".om"
text tc ".c"
text tout ".out"
text tsrc "src/"
text twd "want/"
text tbo "bin/omc/"
text tb2 "bin/cO2/"
text tb0 "bin/cO0/"
text tbn "bin/neg/"
text tfib "fib"
text tsieve "sieve"
text tom2 "om2/"
text tkom2 "/kernels/om2/"
text tnull "/dev/null"
text tcerr "child.err"
text tparan "/proc/sys/kernel/perf_event_paranoid"
text tdir1 "src"
text tdir2 "want"
text tdir3 "bin"
text tdir4 "bin/omc"
text tdir5 "bin/cO2"
text tdir6 "bin/cO0"
text tdir7 "bin/neg"
text tdir8 "src/om2"
text tdir9 "want/om2"
text tdir10 "bin/omc/om2"
text tdir11 "bin/cO2/om2"
text tdir12 "bin/cO0/om2"
text tdir13 "bin/neg/om2"
text tgo2 "/usr/bin/gcc -B/usr/bin/ -O2 -static -o"
text tgo0 "/usr/bin/gcc -B/usr/bin/ -O0 -static -o"
text tsp " "
text tnl "\n"
text tq "'"
text twrong "39088168\n"
text tx "x"
text frt0 "text ta \"39088169\\n\"\nfn main to int\nw = write 1 ta 0 len ta\nret 0\nend\n"
text frtb "text ta \"39088169\\n\"\ntext tb \"12x\\n\"\nfn main to int\nw = write 1 ta 0 len ta\nv = write 2 tb 0 len tb\nret 0\nend\n"
text frt1 "text ta \"39088169\\n\"\ntext tb \"123\\n\"\nfn main to int\nw = write 1 ta 0 len ta\nv = write 2 tb 0 len tb\nret 0\nend\n"
text frtc "fn main to int\nx = argcnt\nif gt x 0\ntrap 5\nend\nret 0\nend\n"
text tfxd "fx/"
text tn0 "nort"
text tnb "badrt"
text tn1 "rt123"
text tnc "crash"
text tfibo "fib.out"
text tkeepw "want.keep"
text tkeep2 "cO2.keep"
text tkeepd "cO2."
text tkeepn "keep"
text tP "P"
text tT "T"
text tH "H"
text tfxs "fx/src.om"
text tdirf "fx"
text rclean "./conductor run 1 0 7 1 4 omc cO2 cO0 neg fib sieve"
text rfib "./conductor run 1 0 7 1 4 omc cO2 cO0 neg fib"
